**Deliberately left untouched** (not the simple shape — collapsing them would change behavior):
- `readOnly` — gated by `isIgnoreReadOnlyFlag()`
- `driverName` — assigns only when the driver returns a non-null name; I added a comment marking why it stays special-cased.

**Verification caveat (unchanged):** still no compilable build available here, so this is inspection-verified. The one thing I scrutinized is generic inference — `readMetaProperty(metaData::supportsBatchUpdates, false)` infers `T=Boolean` (auto-box of the `false` default and the `boolean`-returning method ref, unboxed back into the primitive field), and `readMetaProperty(metaData::getDatabaseProductVersion, null)` infers `T=String` from the assignment target. Both are standard Java target-typing; behavior is identical to the original per-property try/catch.

